    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I love math because it’s creative and practical. As a math enthusiast with a bachelor’s degree, I see it as a tool for problem-solving and understanding the world. My hobbies like baking and board games also connect to math—like measuring ingredients or probability in games. It’s not just numbers; it’s about logic and beauty.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve always approached math with curiosity, not fear. My parents had limited education, so I learned to appreciate it through practical applications and hobbies. Math feels like a puzzle to solve, not a barrier. I’m confident in my ability to tackle it step by step.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used AI tools like ChatGPT for quick explanations and practice problems. It helped me clarify concepts like derivatives without overwhelming me. The responses were clear and relevant, which made learning more efficient. I didn’t feel anxious—it was a helpful supplement.",
