    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized learning paths by adapting to students’ needs, like explaining concepts in simple language or generating practice problems. They can also provide instant feedback on homework, helping students learn at their own pace. This makes math more accessible and less intimidating, especially for those who struggle with traditional methods."
